/Title (Dennis Ndegwa \(Bull\) is a visual artist based in Nairobi, Kenya with over five years experience in Kenya's dynamic and evolving art scene.  Born \(1998\) and raised in Nairobi, my practice is rooted in capturing the rhythms, resilience and resourcefulness of everyday Kenyan life. My art echoes both the vibrancy and grit of my surroundings.  In my recent body of works, I creatively combine acrylics and recycled 'unga' paper drawing inspiration from bodabodas, using them as symbolic vessels for Kenya's economic shifts, urban motion and the relentless grit of its people as they hustle for their daily bread Or 'kutafuta unga' as we call it in the streets. Through the layered surfaces and bold visuals, I explore themes of survival, innovation and the hustle that defines Kenya's social and cultural fabric.  Driven by a desire to document contemporary Kenyan identity, I transform ordinary scenes into vivid narratives. My work not only celebrates the hardworking spirit of those around me but also highlights sustainability through use of repurposed materials. Major Exhibitions Kenya National Museum.  Affordable art show 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025 Art in the Open Village Market Mall.  Group show exhibition 2023, 2024, 2025 Kioko Mwitiki Art Gallery. Red Bull doodle art. Top 30 finalist. March 2023.  Canadian High commission Nairobi.  \(Private Exhibition\) May 2025 Friends of The Arts \(FOTA\) International School of Kenya.  International school of Kenya annual exhibition. 2024, 2025 House of Friends Gallery Kibera Nairobi.  Kibera Art District art biennale \(S.O.S\) 2025 International Leadership University Kenya.  Art Auction November 2025 Solo Exhibition. House Of Friends Gallery.  Solo exhibition \(KUJITUMA\) Annex gallery Kibera February-March 2026.)
